  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Pre-OS Boot / Bootkit — Direct Write to /dev/sda", "technique": "T1542.003", "what_happened": "At 2027-11-18 03:42:08 CET, Linux auditd on linux-baremetal-srv-09 (agent.id=141) captured a write syscall to /dev/sda: data.audit.exe=/usr/bin/dd, data.audit.command='dd if=/tmp/p065_03_20271118_034208/mbr_tampered_20271118_034208.bin of=/dev/sda bs=512 count=1 conv=notrunc', data.audit.uid=0, data.audit.ppid=18922 (parent bash). The audit watch '-w /dev/sda -p w -k mbr_write' was configured fleet-wide as Tier-0. The write was 512 bytes targeting LBA 0 = Master Boot Record. No firmware update or LVM operation was scheduled at 03:42 — this is a malicious MBR overwrite.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 80800 'Auditd: write syscall on /dev/sd* (MBR modification)' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1542.003. Any write to /dev/sd* outside firmware-update / disk-partitioning maintenance windows = high-fidelity bootkit signal.", "first_seen": "2027-11-18T03:42:08+0100"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Pre-OS Boot / TPM PCR[4] Drift Without Firmware Update Window", "technique": "T1542.003", "what_happened": "At 03:42:55 CET (47s after the MBR write), Wazuh's measured-boot agent (tpm2-tools integration) reported a PCR drift artefact written to /var/log/tpm/pcr_drift_20271118_034208.log: data.tpm.pcr_index='4' (IPL Code / bootloader), data.tpm.pcr_baseline='c5d2e8f1a4b3...' (registered at OS install / last known-good), data.tpm.pcr_current='7f3a1b9c2d5e...' (post-MBR-tamper measurement). PCR[0] (BIOS) and PCR[7] (Secure Boot policy) remained UNCHANGED — only PCR[4] (bootloader) drifted, confirming the modification is at the MBR/bootloader layer specifically, not deeper firmware. NO firmware-update change ticket is open for this host (last firmware update CHG-2027-08-14-3, 96 days ago).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 80801 'TPM PCR drift artefact detected' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1542.003 when PCR drift is observed AND no concurrent firmware-update change ticket exists in ServiceNow for this host.", "first_seen": "2027-11-18T03:42:55+0100"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access Vector / Interactive Root Shell from Compromised svc Account", "technique": "context", "what_happened": "auditd's session tree shows ppid=18922 traces back to an interactive SSH login as 'svc_backup' (uid=1003) at 03:39:14, which escalated to root via 'sudo bash' at 03:41:22. The svc_backup account is documented for nightly rsync only — NOT for interactive shell + dd to /dev/sda. The SSH source IP was 10.108.57.184 (NOT an admin jumphost). svc_backup's sudo policy was over-permissive: NOPASSWD ALL = the operator only needed the svc_backup credential to reach root.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh's session-tree decoder correlates auditd auid/sessionid to the SSH parent. The session-tree alert fires as context-only because the SSH login itself was not directly malicious — the abnormality is the COMBINATION of svc_backup + interactive shell + sudo + dd to /dev/sda.", "first_seen": "2027-11-18T03:39:14+0100"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Persistence Confirmation / Survival Across Reboot", "technique": "T1542.003", "what_happened": "At 03:51:22 CET (~9 min after the MBR write), the host rebooted (scheduled or operator-triggered). On the next boot, the bootkit ran BEFORE the kernel: post-boot Wazuh agent reported the same PCR[4] drift value AND an outbound HTTPS connection from the host's egress IP to data.dstip='198.51.100.77' data.dstport=443 within 90s of boot. EDR/AV had not yet initialized at the time of the beacon. This confirms the bootkit is operational and surviving reboots — the LITERAL PDF artefact F 'OSReinstall=Performed / MaliciousBehaviour=Persists' (would persist) and PDF severity 'Persistence survives OS rebuilds' applies.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 80802 'Outbound beacon from server within 5 min of boot with persistent PCR drift' fired with rule.mitre.id=[T1071.001,T1542.003] when the host's post-boot Wazuh-agent rejoin telemetry shows PCR[4] still drifted + outbound to external dst within the 5-min window.", "first_seen": "2027-11-18T03:51:22+0100"}
  ],
